================================================================================
NOTICE - provenance and attribution
================================================================================

This repository is a derivative work. Most of the C++ core, the build system and
the HAPNEST genotype pipeline come from

    virtual-dummies
    Taulant Koka, Jasin Machkour, Daniel P. Palomar, Michael Muma
    https://github.com/taulantkoka/virtual-dummies

    Koka, T., Machkour, J., Palomar, D. P., & Muma, M. (2026).
    Virtual Dummies: Enabling Scalable FDR-Controlled Variable Selection via
    Sequential Sampling of Null Features.

and are used and redistributed here under the GNU General Public License v3,
the license of the upstream project. The full license text is in LICENSE and
applies to this repository as a whole.

What this repository adds is the extension of the virtual dummy construction
from the linear model to score-based forward selection for Bernoulli, Poisson,
multinomial and Cox responses, plus the experiments and the two applications
reported in

    Mehler, H., Koka, T., & Muma, M. (2026).
    FDR-Controlled Variable Selection for Generalized Linear Models with
    Virtual Dummies. Submitted to ICASSP 2026.

The T-Rex selector, which both papers build on, is

    Machkour, J., Muma, M., & Palomar, D. P. (2025). The terminating-random
    experiments selector: Fast high-dimensional variable selection with false
    discovery rate control. Signal Processing, 231, 109894.


